negotiations for a new global climate  change deal are to be finalized at the  Paris conference in December 2015 and  one thing is clear to keep planetary  warming below two degrees centigrade the  richest countries will need to increase  their financial efforts to help  developing countries cut emissions and  adapt to the consequences of climate  change the EU and its member states are  already the largest contributors to  climate finance worldwide at least  twenty percent of EU spending until 2020  has been earmarked for climate related  activities the EU is scaling up  contributions towards the joint  international target of 100 billion US  dollars per year by 2020 to support  climate action in developing countries  but efforts need to be shared in a fair  way amongst developed countries  mobilizing contributions from different  sources promoting green investments  taxing carbon emissions and phasing out  fossil fuel subsidies are all part of  the EU strategy to tackle climate change  but coordinated international action on  climate finance is necessary come out of  the Paris conference with a solid deal  and help developing countries step up  the fight against climate change  you
 

